}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/automatce-full.owl",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology" ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/contributor" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0473-0070"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0744-8855"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1503-4422"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7468-3544"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/creator" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0473-0070"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0744-8855"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1503-4422"
  }, {
    "@id" : "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-7468-3544"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/description" : [ {
    "@value" : "Application ontology for automotive circular-economy product, material, sustainability, usage, dismantling, engineering and transactional data aligned to PMDCore and BFO 2020."
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/license" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce.owl#CC-BY-4.0"
  } ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/title" : [ {
    "@value" : "Automotive Circular Economy Ontology"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionIRI" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/automatce/1.0.0"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo" : [ {
    "@value" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "@value" : "2026-05-28"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Instances of Portions Of Matter whose shape is relevant for their dispostion to participate in a manufacturing process may be (subclasses of) objects that bear a 'blank role' in the context of the manufacturing process."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Material is defined in terms of the three main perspectives that material specifications rely on: the structure of the material (\"intensive quality\"), the performance of the material (\"behavoiral material property\") and the processing the material must have undergone (\"output of some process\").\n\nWhen defining specific materials/material taxonomies, these three aspects shall be taken into account in the aristotelian (\"per genus et differentiam\") as differentiation."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The sum of portions of matter of the same type form a portion of matter of that type."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Material"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "material"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid140"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Portion of Material"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A material is a portion of matter that may participate in some manufacturing process and whose shape is not relevant for its participation in the manufacturing process."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000001",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "It is also representing a distinct physical or conceptual part of a material or substance.\n\nThe open energy ontology OEO defines portion of matter as a subclass of object aggregate, which implies countability. Our portion is not (precisely) countable and thus bearer of intensive properties."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Lome explanation for portion of matter: \"What is a molecule cluster at the cellular level? Contrary to the molecular level, at the cellular level of granularity the boundary of each molecule is outside of the level of granular focus. What forms a discontinuous cluster of countable individual molecules and thus bona fide objects at the molecular level, is a continuous and non-countable molecular substance at coarser levels of\ngranularity. At these coarser levels, the individual molecules cannot be differentiated and demarcated anymore and the cluster as a whole possesses only fiat inner boundaries.\""
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "portion of matter"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000040"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A material entity that is not demarcated by any physical discontinuities. At some finer level of granularity it is an object aggregate, at some coarser level of granularity it is a fiat object part,but at this level of granularity it is neither."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000002",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "We recognize that some of the materials in the subclasses also occur naturally. However, these are not within the scope of our consideration for technical use."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "engineered material"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid152"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid148"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An engineered material is a material that is output of a manufacturing process."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "is subject of"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Inverse of 'is about'."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A property is a material trait in terms of the kind and magnitude of response to a specific imposed stimulus. Generally, definitions of properties are made independent of material shape and size.\n(Callister, W.D., Rethwisch, D.G., Materials Science and Engineering, Wiley, 2014)\n\nTechnical materials are complex aggregates. Many properties that are determined for those aggregates are intrinsically associated with the methodologies employed in the measurement process. This is in contrast to typical 'physical' properties, which like e.g. mass that can be determined to high accuracy independently of the measurement process. \nAs a consequence, material properties in the ontology are differeciated according to their measurement method, e.g. Brinell hardness and Vickers hardness are different types of indentation hardness rather than different measures/quantification (GDC) of the materials property 'indentation hardness'.\n The 'unit idenifieres' of such properties (e.g. \"HV1\", \"HV10\", \"HBW\") are strictly speaking not units but rather references to the measurement methodology used to determine a numeric value that quantifies the property.\n\nExtensive properties that depend on the object being tested rather than on the portion of matter are (extensive) object- or system-properties."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "material property"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000016"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid153"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid154"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "a disposition of a portion of matter that is realized in a compatible process and whose realization is grounded in the portions intensive qualities"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000008",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Process attribute for a process has a similar application to specifically dependened continuant (SDC) for an independent continuant (IC). Furthermore, process attribute describes how SDCs of some participants, i.e., ICs, change in a process. \n\nSpecific rates, e.g., tensile rate, cooling rate, etc. should be added as  subclasses of this class."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "process attribute"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000003"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "process characteristic"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "a process attribute is a dependent occurrent that existentially depends on a process."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Tensile rate in a tensile testing process. Cooling rate in a quenching process"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000075",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en-us",
    "@value" : "mold"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "mould"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A device consisting of a hollowed-out cavity that shapes fluid or plastic material into a specific form through the process of solidification or cooling."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000077",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "specified by value"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000004"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A relation between an entity and a value specification which is about this entity."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000110",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "geological process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A natural process that operates within the Earth system to transform, transport, or deform Earth materials, thereby changing Earth structures and landforms"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000503",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "ASTM grainsize"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020243"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid160"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The ASTM grain size is a quality that is measured through a process that follows the ASTM standard."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000512",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "aggregate state"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid170"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid169"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality representing the physical state of a material, such as solid, liquid, or gasous"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000519",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "flow of electric charge"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "is the process of movement of charged particles"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000520",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "heat flow"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "is a process in which transfer of thermal energy between or within material entities occurs"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000521",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "generation of magnetic field"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "is a process that occurs as a reaction to change of elctric field or movement of charges and produces a magnetic field"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000522",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "mechanical process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "is a process in which forces, moments, or imposed displacements to objects or object aggregates occur and/or the equivalent (stresses, strains) to materials or portions of matter"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000538",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "bulk"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid171"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The bulk is a fiat object part that describes the volume or mass of material considered as a whole, often in contrast to surface or interface phenomena."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000549",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "change of temperature"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "change of temperature is a process in which a particpant changes its temperature"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000551",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "See the editor note of composition to understand the difference between composition and chemical composition.\n\nSee the pattern example of composition to underatand the difference between composition and proportion."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "chemical composition"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The chemical composition is an intensive quality of a portion of matter which describes the types and proportions of pure chemical elements in the portion of matter, and it is a subject of some chemical composition data item."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000553",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "chemical potential"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality of a thermodynamic system describing the energy change associated with the addition of a small quantity of a substance to a system at constant temperature and pressure."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000577",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "composite"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000890"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An object aggregate that consists of two or more bonded materials with dissimilar physical or chemical properties which are used to complement each other where the parts remain seperate and distinct in the resulting object aggregate."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@value" : "carbon fibre reinforced polymer\nlaminated glass\nwood\nhard metal composites for abrasive tools"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Datenverarbeitung"
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Rechenprozess"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "computing process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid175"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A process that involves the systematic use of computational methods and tools to perform simulations, analyses, or data transformations to achieve specific scientific or engineering goals."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein Prozess, der die systematische Verwendung von rechnerischen Methoden und Werkzeugen umfasst, um Simulationen, Analysen oder Datenumwandlungen durchzuführen, um spezifische wissenschaftliche oder technische Ziele zu erreichen."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000591",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The finite set of periodic geometric arrangements is described e.g. by the 14 possible Bravais Lattices in three-dimensional space."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "crystal structure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid181"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid180"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive qualtty of a crystal that embodies the periodic geometric arrangement of entities in a crystal lattice."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000595",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "defect density"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality describing the number of defects per unit volume or area in a material, which can affect its mechanical and electronic properties"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000596",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "deformation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The deformation is a process describing a change in the shape, size, or structure of a material often under the influence of stress or force."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000597",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "density"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The density is a universal intensive quality representing the unit mass of a portion of matter per unit volume."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Gerät"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "device"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000030"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A device is an object that is designed to perform a specific function or task involving measurement, manipulation, processing, or analysis."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein physisches oder virtuelles Objekt, das verwendet wird, um eine bestimmte Funktion oder Aufgabe auszuführen, häufig im Zusammenhang mit der Messung, Manipulation oder Analyse von Materialien."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000618",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "elastic modulus"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000949"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid182"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "represents a material's stiffness, defined as the ratio of stress to strain in the elastic deformation region."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000619",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "electric potential"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020148"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an extensvie quality describing the amount of work needed to move a unit charge from a reference point to a specific location in an electric field."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000629",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "emission of radiation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The emission radiation is a process describing the release of energy in the form of electromagnetic waves or particles from a material."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000635",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "evolution of damage"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An evolution of damage is a process representing the progression of material degradation under mechanical, thermal, or chemical stresses."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000654",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "functional material"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid195"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid187"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A functional material F is an engineered material which has the disposition to be used for an object O (O consists of F) and O's function is other/more than mechanical load carrying."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000661",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "It is often composed of silica-based compounds."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "glass"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A glass is an engineered material present as an amorphous solid typically formed by rapid cooling of a melt."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000663",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "crystallite"
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "kristallit"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Korn"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "grain"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A crystal grain is a crystal that is part of a polycrystal."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000773",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "hardness"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The hardness is a mechanical property used as a measure of a material's resistance to localized plastic deformation, often tested by indentation or scratch methods."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000777",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "heat capacity"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000981"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid200"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The heat capacity is a thermal property describing the amount of heat energy required to raise the temperature of a material by a given amount."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000790",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "e.g., air into glass"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "refraction (optical)"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Optical property which describes the bending of light as it passes from one medium into another due to a change in the light’s speed."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000794",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Spritzgießmaschine"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "injection molding machine"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000602"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An injection molding machine is a device used to produce plastic parts by injecting molten plastic into molds under high pressure."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Eine Spritzgießmaschine ist ein Gerät, das verwendet wird, um Kunststoffteile durch Einspritzen von geschmolzenem Kunststoff in Formen unter hohem Druck herzustellen."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000802",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "absorption of radiation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "process of taking up radiation by a material entity"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Manufacturing processes alternate qualities of materials, i.e., a value specification of some quality of a material entity, which is a specified input to the process, cannot be the same as a value specification of the same quality of another material entity, which is a specified output of the process. \n\nUnfortunately it is not possible to write down such axiom based on OWL. Semi-working solution are the temporally qualified continuants + SPARQL constrains."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Herstellungsprozess"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "manufacturing process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/COB_0000035"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid213"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid217"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid201"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A planned process that is driven by the primary intent to transform objects\nA manufacturing process is always a transformative process."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein geplannter Prozess, der von der primären Absicht angetrieben wird, Objekte zu transformieren. Ein Herstellungsprozess ist immer ein Transformationsprozess."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000845",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "matrix role"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020001"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Matrix is the role of a 'PortionOfConnectedMatter' that implies to host the Filler."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The axiom that mechanical property has realization some application of mechanical load treats only conventional materials and not such effects as magnetostriction etc."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "mechanical property"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid221"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid222"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A mechanical property is a material property which is a characteristic of material M. Mechanical property has realization in a stimulating process (in most cases, application of mechanical load), and the stimulating process is an occurent part of another process, in which an object O that is an instance of M participates."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000851",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "melting point"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020164"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The melting point is a state of matter boundary realized by transition form the solid state to the liquid state (or vice versa)."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000852",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "metal"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid224"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A metal is an engineered material representing a class of materials characterized by high electrical and thermal conductivity, ductility, and metallic bonding."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000853",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "typically observed through crystallographic analysis"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "crystallographic texture"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality describing the arrangement and orientation of grains in a polychrystal"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000868",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "natural organic material"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid245"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid246"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid236"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Natural organic materials are materials derived from natural biological sources, primarily composed of carbon-based compounds."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "material derived from natural biological sources or processes"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000869",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "chemical reaction"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The occurrence of (a) chemical reaction is the process in which substances interact to form new chemical compounds or alter their molecular structure."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000877",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "optical property"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid250"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An optical property is a material property representing the characteristics that describe how a material interacts with light, including reflection, refraction, and absorption."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000882",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "phase boundary (realization)"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A phase boundary is a realizable entity that is realized by the transition between distinct phases."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000888",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "polymer"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000000"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid255"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid251"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A polymer is an engineered material that consists of many repeated subunits (monomers) to form long chains. The atoms within a polymer chain are bonded together by covalent bonds. The intermolecular forces between polymer chains are typically represented by van der waals forces and hydrogen bonds."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000890",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "connected material entity aggregate"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An object aggregate that is a mereological sum of separate material entities, which adhere to one another through chemical bonds or physical junctions that go beyond gravity."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "the atoms of a molecule, the molecules forming the membrane of a cell, the epidermis in a human body"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000891",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "disconnected material entity aggregate"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000027"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "An object aggregate that is a mereological sum of scattered (i.e. spatially separated) material entities, which do not adhere to one another through chemical bonds or physical junctions but, instead, relate to one another merely on grounds of metric proximity. The material entities are separated from one another through space or through other material entities that do not belong to the group."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "a heap of stones, a colony of honeybees, a group of synapses, the trees of a forest, the canopy of a forest, the fish of a shoal, a group of commuters on the subway, the patients in a hospital"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000896",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The pressure is commonly measured in Pascals."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "pressure"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality describing the force exerted per unit area in or on a material."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Urformen"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "primary shaping"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000833"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Primary Forming"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A manufacturing process that creates a defined workpiece from shapeless material by producing cohesion, whereby the characteristic properties of the material become visible in the end product."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein Herstellungsprozess, der aus formlosem Stoff durch das Herstellen von Kohäsion ein definiertes Werkstück schafft, wobei die charakteristischen Eigenschaften des Materials im Endprodukt sichtbar werden."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Casting, Sintering"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000907",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Urformen Aus Dem Plastischen Zustand"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "primary shaping from the plastic state"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000899"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A primary shaping process that involves forming materials from a plastic state."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein Urformprozess, der das Formen von Materialien aus einem plastischen Zustand beinhaltet."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Thermoforming of plastic sheets."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000933",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Simulationsprozess"
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "simulation process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000583"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A computing process that models the behavior of a system over time using mathematical or computational techniques."
  }, {
    "@language" : "de",
    "@value" : "Ein Datenverarbeitungsprozess, der das Verhalten eines Systems im Laufe der Zeit mit mathematischen oder rechnerischen Techniken modelliert"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000942",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "specific surface area"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "an intensive quality embodying the total surface area of a material per unit of mass or volume."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000949",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "stiffness"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid256"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000952"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The stiffness is a material property describing the resistance of a material to deformation under an applied force."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000950",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "stimulating process"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid268"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass" : [ {
    "@id" : "_:genid257"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The stimulating process is a process describing the application of an external influence, such as force, heat, or radiation, to study material response."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000952",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "strength"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000848"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The strength is a material property describing the maximum stress a material can withstand before failure."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000967",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The concept refers to an absolute temperature, not to be mistaken with temperature difference."
  }, {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "To express that an object has a temperature, the property 'intensive bearer of' can be used. It implies a chain of: object consists of some portion of matter and portion of matter bearer of some temperature."
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "temperature"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020131"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The temperature is a fundamental intensive quality representing the average atomic or molcular movement or vibration of a portion of matter."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000981",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "thermal property"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000005"
  }, {
    "@id" : "_:genid276"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A thermal property is a material property representing attributes of a material that describe its behavior under temperature changes, such as thermal conductivity and expansion."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001008",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "absorption of wave radiation"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0000802"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "process of taking up elctromagnetic radiation by a material entity"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001028",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "in response to"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001029"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "inverse of responds with"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001029",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000017"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "responds with"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The realizable entity must be \"stimulated\" by some Stimulus in order to respond with the Response. The bearer of the realizable entity must participate in Stimulation as well as in Response."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001036",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "uncertainty"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000030"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "A quantitative indication of the doubt about a measurement result, expressing the range within which the true value is expected to lie."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0001044",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "date value specification"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0001933"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "A datum that represents a date or time interval associated with another specification."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0010026",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "organic composition"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0025001"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "A composition characterized by a primary molecular structure of carbon atoms covalently bonded to hydrogen (C-H bonds), typically forming linear, branched, or networked chains."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0010033",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "polymerization"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000015"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "The chemical process of reacting monomers, oligomers, or reactive precursors together to form longer macromolecular chains or three-dimensional networks"
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020001",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "filler role"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf" : [ {
    "@id" : "http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000023"
  } ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@language" : "en",
    "@value" : "Filler is the role of a 'PortionOfDisconnectedMatter' that implies being hosted in a matrix."
  } ]
}, {
  "@id" : "https://w3id.org/pmd/co/PMD_0020003",
  "@type" : [ "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class" ],
